# Shell scripts keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This repo ships them as executables rather than as sources someone reads:
# hooks-handlers/ runs from the plugin cache on every session, and
# skills/commit/hooks/commit-msg is copied into each installing repo's
# .githooks/ and run by git. A CR at the end of a line breaks any shell that
# does not tolerate it. Git Bash on Windows happens to tolerate it, which is
# precisely why the breakage would first surface on somebody else's machine
# rather than here.
#
# Nothing else is pinned: Python, Markdown, JSON and the manifests are read by
# parsers that do not care, and forcing them would rewrite every file in the
# working tree for no gain.
*.sh text eol=lf
skills/commit/hooks/commit-msg text eol=lf
